In addition to the new 3D gridded NetCDF file option in PSTFIR and PSTHP,
here is what you need to know about the changes in v3.30

1. Updated all makefile to include support for IFORT and GFORTRAN
	To invoke a different compiler use the syntax: make COMPILER=keyword,
	where keyword is one of pgf90, ifort or gfortran
	The default is PGF90.
	For example, to build all from the main directory using Intel:
		make clean
		make COMPILER=ifort

2. Fixed bug in writing header of CSV file for County/SCC table.

3. Fixed bug in LBASE causing tables to have all zero values.

4. Added GAS/PM flag to /SPECIES LIST/ packet.
	Before:
/SPECIES LIST/
                   :NO         NO             46.0
	After:
/SPECIES LIST/
                   :NO         NO             46.0 GAS
If the flag is missing the default of GAS is used.

5. Added projection parameters (last lines) to /REGION/ packet.

Line 4:  21-30 Number of cells in X direction
Line 4:  31-40 Number of cells in Y direction
Line 5:  1-20  label (ignored)
Line 5:  21-30 Projection type. Acceptable responses are:
               UTM
               LATLON
               RPOLAR
               LAMBERT
               POLAR
               MERCATOR
Line 6+ depend on type of projection:

/REGION/
Domain Origin      :-2412.0   -1620.0
UTM Zone           :0
Cell Width         :36.0       36.0
Number of Cells    :132        82
Projection type    : LAMBERT
Longitude pole     : -97.0
Latitude pole      : 40.0
1st true latitude  : 45.0
2nd true latitude  : 33.0
/END/

	New lines do not need to be included. Defaults are:

 Projection type   : Lambert Conformal
 Longitude Pole    :   -93.000
 Latitude Pole     :    40.000
 1st True Latitude :    45.000
 2nd True Latitude :    33.000
 Number of counties:   30
